<title>UK: Shire to market Hoechst Marion product.</title>
<headline>Shire to market Hoechst Marion product.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Shire Pharmaceuticals said on Thursday it had been appointed by Hoechst Marion Roussel Ltd, the UK subsidiary of the Hoechst AG, to market a new oral corticosteroid.</p>
<p>Shire said it will market Calcort, the new corticosteroid, in the UK and Ireland for 10 years, effective from May 1, with an option for a five-year extension.</p>
<p>The company did not disclose any financial details of the deal.</p>
<p>Oral corticosteroids are used for a wide range of inflammatory conditions like asthma and rheumatoid arthritis.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
